66 (274-5¾) for another record. The 1954 European Champion, he was the favorite. Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/74124"} "Egil Danielsen"] " was also considered a contender, based on a solid 1956 season. Defending champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/79224"} "Cy Young"] " led the qualifiers but would struggle in the final, finishing 11th. Sidło led after three rounds with 79.98 (262-5), which would be his best mark, and would win the silver medal. Then in the fourth round, Danielson launched a low throw that seemed to stay airborne forever, breaking the world record with 85.71 (281-2½)."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "409"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/74124"} "Egil Danielsen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "74.15 (2)"] [:td {} "85.71 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "411"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/74835"} "Janusz Sidło"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]] [:td {} "72.00 (6)"] [:td {} "79.98 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "421"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77692"} "Viktor Tsybulenko"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src 